  "notes": [
    "BOSYTRO B0C591QLNR is 48V, 25A, 1200W. Its DC output goes to the two CL86T AC power terminals. The V4.1 manual accepts DC on these terminals without polarity requirements.",
    "48V must not connect to Octopus MAIN power or Raspberry Pi power. Octopus MOTOR_POWER supports a different voltage range but is unnecessary for this external CL86T setup. The 24V board supply/converter is still to be selected.",
    "All terminal positions shown here are functional diagram positions, not a measured PCB or connector footprint. Use the linked manufacturer pinouts for physical orientation.",
    "Pi communicates with Octopus over USB. STEP and DIR come from empty driver socket M0, with the PF13/PF12 MCU mappings documented; do not use the MOTOR0 coil output connector for these logic signals.",
    "The Octopus uses 5V HCT buffers. CL86T signal inputs require 7\u201320mA. The drawn interface is a requirement placeholder until the actual adapter output and terminals are checked. Set the CL86T signal selector to 5V for a compatible 5V interface.",
    "Use the matched kit motor and encoder harness. Encoder VCC is the driver 5V output to the encoder, not motor supply. ENA terminals remain unconnected in the manufacturer default enabled configuration.",
    "Three rotations require 3 \u00d7 configured input pulses per revolution. The encoder line count is not the microstep setting. Confirm CL86T switches and firmware timing before implementing the repeating motion.",
    "This simulator shows circuit connectivity; it does not energize hardware or validate mains installation. AC input, protective earth, fusing and enclosure are outside this low-voltage diagram."
  ],
